hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20590","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Uthman al-Thaqafi, that a one-eyed man from Thaqif - Qatadah said: He was called Ma'ruf, meaning praised for good, called Zuhayr ibn 'Uthman - that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The wedding feast is a duty, the second day is kindness, and the third day is showing off and hypocrisy."
"20591","'Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Uthman al-Thaqafi, from a one-eyed man from Thaqif - Qatadah said: He was called Ma'ruf; if his name was not Zuhayr ibn 'Uthman, I do not know what his name is - that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The wedding feast on the first day is a duty, the second is kindness, and the third day is showing off and hypocrisy."
